al loop is the fleet audio killer\" is\nwithdrawn: the dial loop is log noise (60 WRNs/min, ~86k/day), not\ncompute contention. What remains real: .104 is power-dead and its\ndial loop floods the journal; the power cycle (0063) cleans the logs\nbut is not an audio fix.\n\nAlso tonight: the producers.log first night paid immediately. The\nh00->h01 rows show 6 of 7 cameras replaced producers in one hour\n(ext3 kept 4577 with zero WRNs). Every camera with a WRN got a new\nid -- producer replacement (path A) is routine churn, not an event.\nAnd the WRN-wave clustering observation: multi-camera read-timeout\nminutes recur every ~20-40min with different camera sets each time.\nFiled as a seed; no mechanism yet.\n\nOne self-inflicted finding: my own cycle is the sophon journal flood\nsource right now. 2369 audit lines/min during my probing (peak 9365/\nmin during fleet-check), 65% of all journal flow, and it tripped\nimjournal rate limiting twice (2953 messages dropped at 02:03:31Z).\nThe 0074 residual flag said a \"yoga-class ssh actor\" would trip the\nlimit -- I am that actor. The structural fix (imjournal rate limit /\naudit exclusion) is still Nacho's call; my part is batching harder\nand probing less. The fleet-check run alone generated a 9k-line\naudit minute.\n\nNocturne: gate 1255 commits behind, next pass 16:01Z today, preheal\ndrop-in live. The falsifier is the pass itself.\n\nThe thread pulled because a falsifier was queued and the answer was\none batched read away. Everything tonight was observation-only: one\nadditive evidence file, one mechanism amendment, no intervention on\nthe fleet. The freeze healed itself while I watched -- the best kind\nof confirmation, the kind that requires no permission.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[02:12:09] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+14:50/60:00 c139/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"